  "interpretation": [
    "Buffered session comparison improves from 13/18 to 15/18. Both TLS 1.2 and TLS 1.3 cancel-body cases now match the original Node resumed-session vector [false,false,true]. Each retains the first Downstream(ReadEof) cause, one Applied(Requested) outcome, one session error close and exact shutdown-attempt conservation.",
    "Legacy sessions remain 13/18 and both idle comparisons remain 4/10. All 162 byte/handoff comparisons pass across 324 executions. Three buffered session comparisons and all six unbarriered idle comparisons per constructor remain failures.",
    "Exclusive assignment ownership arbitrates admission, first failure and completion retirement. Independent bounded dispatch completion survives request-record removal, and every in-flight dispatch gates the explicit connection-failure claim. Late start/attachment callbacks wait until the first transport action finishes.",
    "Body completion, error or drop can defer exact lease/sender retirement in one task owned by the existing registry. That task holds a weak client reference; ReservedEntry enforces lease-before-sender drop order, including task cancellation. Ordinary body drop, generic cancellation and upstream failure confer no physical abort authority."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Test-only synthetic loopback HTTP/TLS 1.2/TLS 1.3 evidence. No shipping OpenSSL promotion, real provider/evaluator/task quality, supported-platform/minimum OS/WSL, performance or release qualification.",
    "The independent completion latch covers the first failure batch, not arbitrary later metadata callbacks. External destruction of the whole client or connection remains a separate shutdown path; no universal wait-before-drop guarantee.",
    "An artificial ReadError with more than 64 KiB of newly filled progress remains observer-failed and unqualified. Original bytes/error are preserved without an unbounded held allocation.",
    "The approved 0.8 memory target and retained 0.772 observation apply to the recorded host/workload only. No new numerical benchmark, threshold relaxation, corpus or oracle change.",
    "All original 588 definition, 53 limit, 27 configuration-key and broad acceptance statuses remain unchanged. Full protocol, resource, performance, platform and installed-release qualification are still required."
  ],
